<!--
  RM_MuttavaqUttaqar.xml                 RimMandrake — CRACKEDLANDS_RULED_CONTENT_1

  Two of the five new Cracked Lands natives ruled at FLOODEDCANYON_BEDAZZLE_
  SITTING_1 (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/cracked_lands_bedazzle_cast_
  2026-09-28.md). Roster wiring (WildAnimals_CrackedLands.xml,
  RM_FloodedCanyon_Biome.xml) is a separate pass per CRACKEDLANDS_RULED_
  CONTENT_1's own file-collision note — not touched here.

  ============================================================================
  RM_Uttaqar — the rock troll, ported as ours
  ============================================================================

  Port of `DA_RockTroll` (Dinonysus's RockTroll mod, workshop 3472275628,
  1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/Animal_RockTroll.xml, read in full this pass).
  Donor numbers kept as baseline per the bible: baseBodySize 4.5,
  baseHealthScale 10, MoveSpeed 3.5, manhunterOnDamageChance 1.0, armor 1.2
  sharp / 0.7 blunt / 0.8 heat, MarketValue 5300, lifeExpectancy 750,
  trainability Intermediate.

  Label ships as "rock troll" (bible: uttaqar-as-label is a batch-4h DRAFT
  the owner passed on twice); defName is RM_Uttaqar per the commission.

  HEDIFF DECISION — self-petrification PORTED, not flagged-and-skipped.
  Read the donor's own DA_BloodPetrification HediffDef (Animal_RockTroll.xml,
  same file) and its HediffGiverSetDef "RockTroll" (HediffGiverSetDefs/
  HediffGiverSets.xml, same mod): both are pure data. The hediff is a plain
  HediffWithComps using three STOCK comp classes (HediffCompProperties_
  Disappears, HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay, HediffCompProperties_
  Effecter) and the giver set uses the STOCK HediffGiver_Bleeding class. No
  donor C# is load-bearing anywhere in this mechanic, so this is case (a):
  ported as RM_UttaqarPetrification (five stages, same severity/stage shape
  as the donor) + RM_UttaqarPetrificationGivers (HediffGiverSetDef), wired
  onto race.hediffGiverSets below. Colour/labels re-voiced ("wound-stone")
  per the bible's "old uttaqar are effectively walking petroglyphs" framing.

  DORMANT-DISGUISE DECISION — FLAGGED AND SKIPPED, not ported. The donor's
  cousin mechanic (`DA_HibernatingRockTroll`, a RockBase "strange stone
  formation" a troll emerges from) depends on
  `EmergingAnimals.CompProperties_RockCamo` and `EmergingAnimals.
  CompProperties_EmergingAnimal` — compiled classes from a separate donor
  framework mod (EmergingAnimals), not data, and not something this pass may
  invent C# to replace. Per the brief's rule ("if the donor's hediff/comp
  needs compiled behavior you can't replicate data-only, ship without it and
  flag"), RM_Uttaqar ships with NO dormant-disguise rock-formation cousin
  this pass. OWED to a follow-up mechanics pass (CRACKEDLANDS_MECHANICS_
  BUILD_1 is the filed item for this biome's C#-bearing mechanisms; the
  disguise cousin is not yet itemised inside it as of this write — whoever
  claims it should add a line).

  DROPPED per the standing port rule (donor-framework comps/items come out,
  stats/body/form stay — RM_Aurrok.xml precedent):
  - `WanderPreference.MountainPreference` and `EmergingAnimals.
    CompProperties_RockCamo` comps (both donor framework C#).
  - PawnKindDef abilities `DA_GiantRockThrow`/`DA_CrushingSlam` and
    specialTrainables `DA_BoulderThrow`/`DA_CrushingSlam` — donor-defined
    AbilityDefs/TrainableDefs we do not own; kept only the plain Odyssey
    core trainables (AttackTarget, Dig) the donor also listed.
  - `leatherDef DA_Leather_RockTroll` and `butcherProducts DA_Sangonite` —
    both donor-specific ThingDefs this mod does not depend on. Substituted
    vanilla `Leather_Heavy` (matches RUT_SealedSleeper/RM_Aurrok precedent)
    and dropped the bespoke butcherProducts line — default meat+leather
    yield only, no invented resource.
  - Tool capacity `DA_DemolishTroll` (donor ToolCapacityDef) on the head
    tool — substituted vanilla `Blunt`, matching the Aurrok head-tool shape.
  - Body `DA_BipedalAnimalWithClaws` (donor BodyDef, EmergingAnimals-mod
    adjacent) — substituted the closest vanilla claws body,
    `QuadrupedAnimalWithClawsTailAndJowl` (Core/Bodies_Animal_Quadruped.xml),
    rather than importing another donor BodyDef for a silhouette detail.
  - Sound cues `DA_Pawn_RockTroll_*` (donor SoundDefs) — substituted the
    vanilla Rhinoceros set (Pawn_Rhinoceros_Wounded/Death/Call/Angry), the
    closest "heavy armored beast" vanilla voice.

  ART: no render exists for "uttaqar"/"rock troll" tied to this biome (this
  commission owes it, per the bible — not FOUNDRY's fill_queue.py this
  pass). TEMP PLACEHOLDER: the donor's own texture path
  (Animal/RockTroll/RockTroll), same loud-donor-texture-as-placeholder
  convention RM_Aurrok.xml uses.

  ============================================================================
  RM_Muttavaq — the pan giant (invented, no donor)
  ============================================================================

  Authored from the bible's own "Stats sketch" paragraph — no donor def.
  baseBodySize 5.0, baseHealthScale 12, MoveSpeed 2.0, manhunterOnDamageChance
  0 (awake and asleep, per the bible: "it never hunts, never raids, never
  manhunters" and "damage while waking it is answered by the wake itself, not
  by rage"), Wildness 1.0, untrainable, lifeExpectancy in centuries (320,
  concrete number per the brief).

  WAKE-COMP DECISION — flagged and skipped, per the brief. The bible's real
  wake mechanism (`CompWaterWakeTrigger` family scaled to giant size,
  FlowWorks depth edits on its feeding trail) is explicitly "the mechanics
  item's C#, not this document's" — CRACKEDLANDS_MECHANICS_BUILD_1's scope.
  Shipped here: stock `CompProperties_CanBeDormant` (startsDormant true) only,
  same as the brief asked. As an INTERIM, testable trigger only — same
  posture RUT_SealedSleeper.xml's header used while its own real wake comp
  was being built — added stock `CompProperties_WakeUpDormant` with
  `wakeUpOnDamage=true` so a quicktest can wake and inspect one without the
  real C# landing first; this is NOT the bible's water-wake mechanism and
  should be left alongside it, not replaced, once RM_CompWaterWakeTrigger
  (or its giant-scale equivalent) exists. `receivesSignals=true` set on the
  ThingDef per CompProperties_CanBeDormant.ConfigErrors (required whenever
  jobDormancy is false).

  CRACK-WAX YIELD: mirrors RUT_SealedSleeper.xml's own mechanism exactly —
  a `butcherProducts` shorthand entry, scaled up from the sleeper's 2 to 200
  ("the planet's largest single crack-wax deposit... a fortune in crack-wax
  and meat"). The sheet's actual "wake sheds a ground-drop" behaviour is the
  wake comp's job (owed, see above) — this butcherProducts line is the
  always-available second source, same "second, always-available source"
  role RUT_CrackWax.xml's own header describes for the sleeper.

  NOT A HERD ANIMAL: wildGroupSize min/max 1 (one per pan, pans rare).
  Intended roster commonality ~0.02-0.05 per the bible — noted here for
  whoever wires WildAnimals_CrackedLands.xml; not set by this file.

  ART: no render exists ("this commission" owes it, per the bible). TEMP
  PLACEHOLDER: vanilla Thrumbo texture path as a plausible large-creature
  stand-in, flagged loudly below — swap the instant real art lands.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ======================= RM_Uttaqar — hediff first, referenced by the race below ======================= -->

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RM_UttaqarPetrification</defName>
    <label>wound-stone</label>
    <defaultLabelColor>(163,65,65)</defaultLabelColor>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <description>Near-instant clotting that ossifies into dense, stone-like formations wherever an uttaqar is wounded — the same process the crag giants use in place of scars. Provides ablative protection and slows blood loss while it lasts; old uttaqar carry layers of it like tree rings.</description>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <minSeverity>0.1</minSeverity>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_Disappears">
        <disappearsAfterTicks>60000</disappearsAfterTicks>
      </li>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>10</severityPerDay>
      </li>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_Effecter">
        <stateEffecter>Berserk</stateEffecter>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.1</minSeverity>
        <label>minor</label>
        <becomeVisible>false</becomeVisible>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.15</minSeverity>
        <label>minor</label>
        <statFactors>
          <IncomingDamageFactor>0.9</IncomingDamageFactor>
        </statFactors>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.1</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.30</minSeverity>
        <label>moderate</label>
        <statFactors>
          <IncomingDamageFactor>0.6</IncomingDamageFactor>
        </statFactors>
        <totalBleedFactor>0.8</totalBleedFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.2</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.60</minSeverity>
        <label>severe</label>
        <statFactors>
          <IncomingDamageFactor>0.5</IncomingDamageFactor>
        </statFactors>
        <totalBleedFactor>0.5</totalBleedFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.3</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.80</minSeverity>
        <label>extreme</label>
        <statFactors>
          <IncomingDamageFactor>0.5</IncomingDamageFactor>
        </statFactors>
        <totalBleedFactor>0</totalBleedFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.3</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <HediffGiverSetDef>
    <defName>RM_UttaqarPetrificationGivers</defName>
    <hediffGivers>
      <li Class="HediffGiver_Bleeding">
        <hediff>RM_UttaqarPetrification</hediff>
      </li>
    </hediffGivers>
  </HediffGiverSetDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Uttaqar</defName>
    <label>rock troll</label>
    <description>A colossal, eyeless creature that owns the Cracked Lands' crag walls, talus slopes and slot-canyon dark the way the muttavaq owns the flats — it surfaces from its lair only when provoked. Lacking real regeneration, it answers every wound with stone: ultra-fast clotting ossifies into dense ablative formations within minutes, so an old uttaqar reads as more rock than flesh, seamed with wound-stone in layers a Farmer can count like tree rings.</description>
    <receivesSignals>true</receivesSignals>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>3.5</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>5300</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-55</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>80</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>1.2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.7</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.8</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <PainShockThreshold>1</PainShockThreshold>
      <IncomingDamageFactor>0.8</IncomingDamageFactor>
      <InjuryHealingFactor>2</InjuryHealingFactor>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Wildness>0.80</Wildness>
      <FilthRate>8</FilthRate>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities>
          <!-- Substituted vanilla Blunt for the donor's DA_DemolishTroll
               ToolCapacityDef (donor-only def) — see header. -->
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>20</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>true</ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>left claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
          <li>Stab</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>17</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.3</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftClaws</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>right claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
          <li>Stab</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>17</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.3</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightClaws</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>23</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.3</cooldownTime>
